{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"allstar-holy-hairstreak","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nTime-sensitive operational issues — `rebar-*` CloudWatch alarms and failures of scheduled/`main`-branch GitHub Actions workflows — are found today only by a human-launched sweep session (ledger `tomophobic-stilllife-mayfly`, `docs/user-guide.md` \"Ops error-sweep ledger\"). A session holding a ticket `in_progress` is never told when another session comments on, edits, closes, or takes over that ticket: `cross_session_warning` (`src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py`) warns the *actor*, not the holder, and is silent over the MCP server because `claimed_session` is stamped from `resolve_session_id()` in the *server's* environment (`src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:71`). There is no project-wide, time-bound notice (outage, quiet window, maintenance) that every session sees.\n\nResearch (2025-26 OSS) fixed the shape: server→client MCP push is unsupported by every target harness (Claude Code #7252/#36665 closed not-planned; Codex #15299/#17543 open; Cursor subscribe errors), so delivery is at boundaries — piggybacked on tool responses (Kubernetes `Warning:` header, Slack `response_metadata.warnings`, git `advice`) plus harness hooks. Trackers auto-subscribe on assign with a typed `reason` (GitHub Notifications API). Incident tools dedup on a curated fingerprint and treat re-fire-after-close as `regressed` (Sentry). This store's own history demands that last rule: of 24 canary-filed bugs, most are serial duplicates from auto-close + re-fire (nine `[binding-drift]` tickets in 14 days).\n\n## Approach\n\nOne shared **inbox delivery layer** — a per-session cursor, dedup, a hard byte cap, rendered on all three seams: an appended MCP text content block outside every tool's `outputSchema` (the registrar-proxy seam at `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:674-681`), CLI stderr lines with stdout and exit code untouched, and a library read API plus warning channel (`src/rebar/_lib_warn.py`). Three independent **read-time producers** feed it from the existing event log, so no broadcast queue and no per-delivery commit: (1) changes on tickets the session holds (auto-subscribed at claim) and on subscribed tags; (2) active advisory `notice` tickets — a new first-class type with typed `starts_at`/`ends_at`/`severity`/`suppress` carrying `session_log`'s carve-outs, expiry evaluated in the active-now query; (3) `ops-alert` bugs filed by a portable `rebar alerts ingest` operation under `docs/bug-creation-contract.md` plus eight anti-noise rules (dedup survives close for 14 days and reopens as regressed; recovery is a comment, never an auto-close; flap damping; N≥2 observations; `suppress` notices honored; storm grouping; per-run and per-day filing caps; ≤1 accumulation comment per 24h). Alert announcements reach only sessions subscribed to the tag; `claim` is the acknowledgement. Identity over MCP is the authenticated principal sub-partitioned by a client-supplied session hint, never across principals.\n\nPositive rationale: boundary delivery is the only channel the harnesses honor; read-time producers reuse the event log rebar already syncs; a typed notice avoids parsing expiry out of prose (the GitLab stale-banner failure); the identity model keeps the existing auth trust boundary (`src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:63` `PROXY_IDENTITY` ContextVar) intact. Scope is the notification system only: advisory notices, no enforcement, no claim TTL/release, no NOT-A-BUG registry — those are linked follow-on ideas.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A session that claimed a ticket over MCP or the CLI receives, at its next tracker interaction on any seam, one line per change another session made to that ticket (comment, edit, status change, claim lost, closed, link, tag) with a typed reason; proxy: the delivery child's cross-seam tests pass (CLI subprocess, library call, MCP in-process client).\n- [ ] An operator can post a notice with a window; every session sees it once per session while active and never after `ends_at`; proxy: the notice child's read-time expiry tests and CLI/MCP/library round-trip tests pass.\n- [ ] A new `rebar-*` alarm transition or allowlisted workflow failure becomes exactly one open `ops-alert` bug per fingerprint; a re-fire within 14 days of close reopens that same ticket; repeats add at most one comment per 24h; proxy: the ingester child's fixture-driven dedup/regression/flap/storm tests pass.\n- [ ] Alert announcements are delivered only to sessions subscribed to `ops-alert`; an unsubscribed session gets no alert line; proxy: the subscription tests in the delivery child pass.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The scheduled ingester has run against the live CloudWatch and GitHub Actions sources without filing any duplicate: the operator records the run id, its report counts, and the timestamp as a ticket comment on the scheduling child.\n- [ ] The runbook and agent guidance tell a monitoring or debugging session how to subscribe and how notices are posted; proxy: the documented commands exist and the docs-drift gate passes.\n\n## Child decomposition\n\n- **MCP session identity** — principal + session hint resolved on the server, `claimed_session` stamped over MCP, `cross_session_warning` live over MCP, client-config recipes. The foundation every other child consumes.\n- **Inbox delivery + watched-ticket/subscription producer** — the `inbox` operation on three seams, cursors, caps, auto-subscribe on claim, `subscribe`/`unsubscribe`, `inbox.schema.json`. Delivers AC 1 and 4.\n- **`notice` ticket type + `notice post/list/cancel` + active-notice producer + `suppress` field** — delivers AC 2.\n- **Alert ingestion operation** — `rebar alerts ingest` with sources, fingerprinting, the anti-noise rules, ledger watermark, run report. Delivers AC 3.\n- **Scheduled ingestion** — the GitHub Actions cron with a read-only AWS role and the live dry-run proof before codifying. Delivers AC 5.\n- **Harness shims + runbooks/docs** — delivers AC 6.\n\nOrdering: identity → inbox delivery → {notice, ingestion operation} → scheduled ingestion → shims/docs.","id":"44a9-92b4-831c-4a92","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["notifications","ops-alert","brainstorm"],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Session notification system: inbox feed for watched tickets, time-bound notices, and subscribed alert surfacing across MCP, CLI, and library"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788560993940713001,"uuid":"fdc668b3-aefd-41b9-b42e-0ef8a6072b96"}